s that these these failures  to do the right thing to keep others  from doing the wrong thing or to protect  those who are vulnerable to harm or  injury or insult from from being harmed  is in fact quite culpable and so this is  something that we ought to take quite  seriously the other thing that he tells  us about this is a little bit later on  and it's kind of an inquiry as well why  do people fail in this duty to protect  those who are perhaps not only  vulnerable but for whom they're  responsible why do bosses not protect  their employees why do parents not  protect their children why did children  not protect their parents later on why  do we allow other people to to injure to  insult to to humiliate people who we  could protect so he gives us a whole  list of these and a lot of these you  know we might want to look at the Latin  terms a little bit he says that some  people do it out of a sort of reluctance  and he names three things that we might  be reluctant to have to engage with  they're they're kind of a pain for us we  we don't want to deal with that and the  word dealing with here in the Latin  translation there's a little bit more  old-fashioned that we have is to incur  right but but the Latin is so skipping  right to endure to have to deal with it  you have to you know ender is is another  word as well and so one of these is  hostility or hatred from other people  who's going to be hostile towards us  well if we if we keep those who are say  exploiting workers from exploiting those  workers if we  call attention to it we say you're doing  the wrong thing they may in fact get  angry with us they may resist us they  may say that we're the bad guys  similarly if we get in you know in  between somebody who's beating up  another person that person may turn on  us and try to attack us as well and so a  lot of people say I just don't want to  get involved it's not really my fight  it's not my thing but but the issue is  that they're they're really acting out  of a sense of fear fear of what is going  to happen to them  trouble you know some other issues may  come out of it should I get involved in  the fight between the big guy and the  little guy well but might I might get  messed up you know I just finished tying  it should I really get in there and  start you know duking it out with  someone I don't know you know if I had  like you know my gym clothes on then of  course I'd be in there fighting for them  well I mean we can come up with all  sorts of examples of that and so this is  when it calls labora right it takes work  on our part then we have expense well I  would get involved but I don't want to  pay for that and and you know if you  think about the opportunities that we  have in the West to make life better or  or simply to prevent wrong prevent harm  prevent you know unjust relations by  spending a little bit of money  I think cicero's discussion here  actually bears a lot of fruit he talks  in terms of what it is that we have to  pay what it is that we have to be  willing to shell out so that's one big  reason a sort of reluctance to deal with  these sorts of things he also talks  about you know he's using synonyms here  indifference  laziness sluggishness the last word  there is in there see how the word that  we get inertia from it means a  unwillingness to get up and do something  the first one is actually  negly giggle agencia  and and this can mean indifference it  can also mean a not caring you know  which you might say well that is being  indifferent but it is it's not caring  about what we ought to care about when  we say that somebody is negligent that's  what we have in mind they are negligent  by not caring about things that they  ought to care about it could be how  their appearance affects other people  right or it could be about what somebody  else saying or doing will you know what  sort of impact that will have on  somebody else and as Cicero of course  it's not saying that we have to like be  as you know people like to say these  days snow flakes about this or assume  that everybody else is snow flakes but  we know when certain lines have been  crossed if somebody is whoring another  person they probably shouldn't be doing  that if we see somebody bullying another  person whether physically or emotionally  verbally we know that that shouldn't be  going on if we see sexual harassment  taking place we shouldn't say that I  don't really care about that sort of  thing Cicero says we should be ready to  take whatever steps are necessary the  other one that he says that's really  interesting has to do with what we can  call preoccupation or self focus that  the Latin translation here has  self-interest but I think being focused  on one's own self is probably a better  way to talk about he says you know oh  Cappuccio is is is something that  intervenes preoccupation a little bit  later on he will talk about our own  business you know Nageotte sia as being  what it is so the things that preoccupy  us the things that we take is worthy of  doing can sometimes become impediments  to doing justice to actually protecting  people when we should we can say you  know I've got all this grading to do so  I can't really respond to this email  even though I probably should you know  I've kept my own work that I have to  concentrate on if I just do my own stuff  and I stick with my job this other stuff  will sort itself out or if it doesn't  it's not really my problem we might say  similarly about people within a family  you know if if you know that that your  child is having trouble in school and  you say well you know that's why I send  them to school so the school can handle  that sort of stuff I really have to  focus on the house or on my business or  on this other relationship over here  because because you know I've got to  make money in order to make this this  happen anyway so that's that's one thing  and then he talked about what we're  calling herself focus yeah that's the  oka pottsfield  studious as well the things that we are  zealous about the things that we take  care about you know if being a concert  violinist and putting in the hours and  hours of practice means that you have to  neglect your duties to protect other  people sister would say that's a problem  so we could go on and on with other  examples the last one that he talks  about that that's particularly  interesting is aversion to our fellow  human beings sometimes we just want to  be left the hell alone and we don't  really like spending time with these  other people he says oh do quote um  homing them swim right you know that we  don't like other other people and that  that allows us to to justify to  ourselves the fact that other people are  harming them they're jerks anyway they  got it coming to them we don't have to  be concerned with them now I do want to  point out one other thing back to this  this preoccupation this being concerned  with one's own projects one one's own  personal development cicero actually  criticized  other philosophers here he says there is  reason to fear that what Plato declares  of the philosophers may be inadequate  when he says that they are just because  they're busied with the pursuit of truth  and because they despise and count as no  not that which most men eagerly seek and  for which they are prone into battle  against each other for the death Plato  is saying look philosophers are great  because they're not going to get into  everybody else's business they're so  busy you know reading their books  thinking about the universe you know  writing books teaching classes doing all  that sort of stuff they stay out of  everybody else's hair Cicero thinks  maybe they should get into everybody  else's hair if they're so distracted by  their intellectual pursuits that they're  neglecting their human duties to protect  the weak the vulnerable the needy to not  allow injustice to be done to them then  they themselves appear to be unjust and  so he goes on and he says to secure one  sort of justice that's what they do but  they fall into the opposite injustice  hampered by their pursuit of learning  they leave to their fate those whom they  ought to defend he says Plato thinks  they won't even assume their civic  duties except under compulsion that this  is in fact what they ought to do so  Cicero is an advocate of what we call  the active life or a mixed life where  intellectual pursuits are coupled with  fulfilling duties in an active way and  that is going to include taking care of  other people and protecting them from  injustice failure to do so for any of  these motives makes one unjust  you
 

